{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-09T19:25:14.594Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"9dcd842323ed26e7b36c7b86","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"Issue: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/issues/228. The dispatch step polls until it can land the PR (7200 s with github.token, 2400 s with an app token, over 120/40 attempts). The caller CI it waits for needs runners from the same free-tier account pool: between 10:00Z and 12:00Z on 2026-11-09, 77 fleet runs queued while 8 ran; a scheduled sync sat in that step from 10:27Z, holding a runner while waiting for CI that could not start. An automation job must never wait in-job for work that competes for the same runner pool.\n\nPlan: dispatch caller CI, arm GitHub native auto-merge on the owned PR, report parked runs and exit. When auto-merge cannot be armed (GITHUB_TOKEN mode, no branch protection, disabled setting), print a notice with the reason; the next scheduled sync lands the PR. Remove the whole polling class from both reusable workflows (sync and closeout), add timeout-minutes to every reusable job, add a contract test that fails on revert."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-github-fxhd"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The gated sync holds a runner for up to two hours while it waits for caller CI it competes with for the same pool"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":""},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-09T19:25:14.594Z"},{"op":"add","path